Phoenix-RTOS: wire the phoenix video + input driver into the build.

Adds the phoenix video driver (src/video/phoenix/, copied into the tree by the
port's p_prepare overlay step) to the PHOENIX cmake branch and enables desktop
OpenGL. The driver is one always-fullscreen /dev/fb0 window rendered by the
in-process ported Mesa V3D GL stack, with keyboard/mouse drained from
/dev/kbd0 + /dev/mouse0 in PumpEvents. SDL_VIDEO_DRIVER_PHOENIX gates the driver
sources + the SDL_config.h define + the bootstrap-table entry (placed first, so
it is auto-selected ahead of the dummy driver). SDL_VIDEO_OPENGL turns on SDL's
desktop-GL attribute plumbing (it uses SDL_GL_GetProcAddress internally, so it
adds no direct GL link dependency to libSDL2.a).

The GL-context bring-up itself (Mesa state-tracker + V3D winsys, which needs
Mesa-internal headers this cross build never sees) lives OUTSIDE libSDL2.a in a
separately-compiled glue TU that the game links; the driver references its
plain-C entry points as unresolved externs. This keeps libSDL2.a pure zlib.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt	2026-08-04 23:18:49.141588853 +0200
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt	2026-08-04 23:19:00.078554853 +0200
@@ -1474,6 +1474,23 @@
   endif()
   CheckPTHREAD()
 
+  # Phoenix-RTOS video + input driver (SDL2 port plan phase 1, step 4). A single
+  # always-fullscreen window backed by /dev/fb0 (geometry from the RPI4FB_GETMODE
+  # ioctl), rendered with the in-process ported Mesa V3D OpenGL stack (no EGL/GLX);
+  # input is drained from /dev/kbd0 (raw 8-byte HID) and /dev/mouse0 (4-byte HID)
+  # in PumpEvents. The GL-context bring-up itself (Mesa state-tracker + V3D winsys)
+  # lives OUTSIDE libSDL2.a in a separately-compiled glue TU that the game links
+  # (it needs Mesa-internal headers this cross build never sees); the driver only
+  # references its plain-C entry points as unresolved externs. See the port's
+  # glue/ directory and the SDL2 port plan for the licensing note on that glue.
+  if(SDL_VIDEO)
+    set(SDL_VIDEO_DRIVER_PHOENIX 1)
+    set(SDL_VIDEO_OPENGL 1)
+    file(GLOB VIDEO_PHOENIX_SOURCES ${SDL2_SOURCE_DIR}/src/video/phoenix/*.c)
+    list(APPEND SOURCE_FILES ${VIDEO_PHOENIX_SOURCES})
+    set(HAVE_SDL_VIDEO TRUE)
+  endif()
+
 elseif(UNIX AND NOT APPLE AND NOT RISCOS AND NOT HAIKU)
   if(SDL_AUDIO)
     if(SYSV5 OR SOLARIS OR HPUX)
